rows.en:
You think he saw an illusion?
To anyone looking on, it's only natural to think he'd lost his mind.
In fact, only the chosen can see that doll.{p}

But people with a strong sixth sense can apparently feel the doll's presence and its eerie aura.
I've seen one too, though not that doll.
An illusion of a doll...{p}

"Well then, shall we head home?
{f:We can't just keep waiting for the seventh person.|It wouldn't do to keep waiting for the seventh person.}"
{f:I|I} said, urging everyone to leave.
We hadn't collected all seven stories, {f:but|but} for now there was plenty of material for a newspaper article{f:.|.}
"Well, I'll be going, then..."
The student who was the last storyteller left.{p}

...{f:Yes|Yes}, this was...
{f:I|I} understood at once.{p}This child was the doll Arai had told us about...
And at the same time, that {f:I|I} was the next sacrifice...{p}

{f:I|I} instinctively shook my hand.
A whole fistful of hair was stuck to it{f:.|.}
It was a little too stiff to be human hair{f:.|.}

{f:I|I} didn't stop him, and watched him go.
...It wasn't a very pleasant story{f:.|.}
To think that every year, one sacrifice has to be offered up to the doll.
If the story is true, then any of us here could be that one{f:.|.}{p}
